@title  PCSE00023 - keep pressing on, to walk through several fights and stages
@game   PCSE00023
@shot-every 40

# WHAT THIS RECIPE IS FOR
# ----------------------
# The RENDER rig for this title. It presses cross every 150 frames, which is enough to
# walk the front end, pick fighters and play through several fights on several stages -
# so one run visits a broad flat ground (the rooftop), a lit interior and a bumpy
# outdoor stage without any of them being scripted by name.
#
# FRAME 3000 IS THE ROOFTOP: flat, light, low camera. It is the clearest reproduction
# there is of anything that goes wrong between a character and the ground it stands on,
# because a shallow floor plane amplifies a small depth error into whole screen pixels.
# That frame is what found the clip-fixup defect that ate ~22 pixels off every boot.
#
# There is no NAVIGATION here and there is not meant to be: a fixed cadence of one
# button walks further into this title than a hand-authored menu path does, and it does
# not go stale when a screen's timing moves.
#
0: @todo no @assert yet - this recipe is judged by its shots, so conformance has nothing
0: @todo to check. A watched round timer or health value would give it one.

